<title>UK: EBRD adds 50 bln lire to 10-year structured bond.</title>
<headline>EBRD adds 50 bln lire to 10-year structured bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 200 billion lire from 150 billion lire, joint lead managers Banca di Roma and Morgan Stanley said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN BANK FOR RECONSTRUTION AND DEVELOPMENT</p>
<p> AMT   *200 BLN ITL   COUPON   **10 PCT    MATURITY ***27.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE   FIX/REV FRN   ISS PRICE  101.125   PAY DATE    27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.50     SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  1.625</p>
<p> NOTES     *LAUNCHED FOR 150 BILLION LIRE ON 11.FEB.97</p>
<p>	   **FOR FIRST THREE YEARS THEN 19.5 PCT MINUS TWO TIMES</p>
<p>	     SIX-MONTH LIBOR.</p>
<p>	  ***CALLABLE AT PAR ON 27.MAR.00</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
